      "year": 2012,
      "set": "7.2",
      "title": "Toy Town",
      "sourceText": "Toy town Hong Kong has been making many of the world’s toys for the past 60 years, and while production takes place in Chinese factories, it is still Hong Kong companies which are responsible for the action figures, dolls, and remote-controlled cars placed under Christmas trees the world over. “Seventy percent of global toy products are made by Hong Kong-run companies,” says Mr. Yeung, the executive vice president of the Toy Manufacturers Association of Hong Kong. A new exhibition organized at the Hong Kong Design Institute of more than 1,000 Hong Kong-made toys will showcase the territory’s toy-making roots and may eventually lead to a permanent museum. It features all types of playthings, from rare Qing dynasty figurines to the Cabbage Patch dolls and Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles produced during the industry’s 1980s heyday and the latest digital toys that hook up to iPods and iPhones. But with kids turning to non-traditional playthings such as video games, computers, music, and cosmetics at younger ages, some say toy manufacturing may be a sunset industry. That is something that Mr. Yeung can’t bring himself to agree with. “As long as there are kids, they will need toys to play with.” Your group is working on a project on the changing trends of toys and games in Hong Kong. Discuss with your group what to include in the project. You may want to talk about:",
      "groupDiscussion": [
        "Whether traditional toys and games are still popular",
        "The advantages of non-traditional toys compared to traditional toys and games",
        "What kinds of toys and games will be popular in the future"
      ],
      "individualResponse": [
        "What was your favourite toy or game when you were growing up?",
        "Do you still have toys or games from when you were a child?",
        "Do you think Hong Kong should open a toy museum?",
        "What qualities do you look for when you buy a toy or game?",
        "Do you think children should have more time to play with toys or games?",
        "Are there toys or games that parents wouldn’t want their children to play with?",
        "Do you think that as a result of high-tech toys, children are growing up more quickly than before?",
        "Do you think that Hong Kong toy manufacturers deserve more recognition?"
      ]
