      "set": "1.1",
      "title": "Selfie Shutter",
      "sourceText": "2015 – 1.1 Selfie Shutter Ever dreamed of taking hands-free selfies? Designed in Hong Kong, the Selfie Shutter (HK$300, available at Studio A – Mong Kok) is a remote Bluetooth shutter to help get rid of that annoying selfie arm from your shots. Stand your phone up on this stand and click away. It’s small and easy to carry around. Selfy iOS Selfy iOS (HK$8, available at itunes.apple.com) provides a similar service to Selfie Shutter by giving you a timer. As an added bonus, it comes with a built-in effects editor. Android users might want to look at the free app, YouCam, which offers a similar set of features. Selfie Stick If you’re looking to take group shots or simply want to take in more of the view behind you, try one of these selfie sticks (HK$350, DG Lifestyle Store, Pacific Place, Admiralty). It is highly portable, only 23 cm long, and when extended reaches 93 cm. Pair with Selfy iOS or YouCam and you should have the perfect selfie set-up. N1 Mini The N1 Mini (HK$4,000) is a smartphone for selfie fans which has a rotating camera with a 195-degree angle. Its main purpose seems to be to get a better angle of yourself without moving your hand. For any selfie obsessives, the “beautify” mode will give you a slimmer face and clearer skin. As members of your school’s Photography Club, your group is planning to give a talk about ‘selfies’ and to recommend two of the pieces of equipment above to take better ‘selfies’. You may want to talk about:",
